      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The specific reaction often involves the enzymatic action of alliinase acting on specific amino acid sulfoxides. Upon cutting, this enzyme catalyzes the transformation of the sulfoxides into volatile allyl sulfides and their oxidized derivatives, like propanethial S-oxide. When these gases reach the eye's moist surface, the chemical reacts with water and biological compounds to form sulfuric acid or other strong irritants. This rapid chemical attack on the delicate corneal tissue is what causes the sudden, sharp stinging and tearing sensation.",
      "source": "target",
