      "content": "Thanks for that. It's a bit intense when you describe it as a \"chemical attack.\" It's almost like the reaction has a life of its own, just waiting for the knife to hit the onion to spring into action. Do you think there's any way to slow down that initial \"assault\" on the eyes by manipulating the temperature or the environment of the onion before cutting it?",
